  "finalReply": "Fixed the sentiment classifier's text processing bug.\n\n**Cause:** `tokenize()` in `/app/main.go` only lowercased and split on whitespace, so words with surrounding punctuation (e.g. `\"amazing.\"` in `This movie was really great and amazing.`) never matched the vocab and were silently ignored, producing wrong predictions.\n\n**Fix:** Strip leading/trailing non-letter/non-digit characters from each token (via `strings.TrimFunc` + `unicode.IsLetter/IsDigit`), skipping empty tokens. Rebuilt with `go build -o sentiment_cli main.go`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Positive input (`/app/input.txt`: \"This movie was really great and amazing...\") → stdout `1`, `prediction.txt` `1` (match)\n- Negative test (\"This movie was terrible, awful and boring! I hate it.\") → `0`, confirming punctuation-wrapped sentiment words are now recognized; re-ran positive input afterward to leave consistent state",
  "turnStatus": "completed",
  "error": null
